    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "one by one",
      "definition": "used before a singular noun to talk about every person or thing in a group, thought of separately rather than as a group",
      "explanation": "**Each** goes directly before a singular noun: *each student*, *each box*. It works for a group of two or more, and it looks at the members one at a time, unlike **every**, which usually treats a larger group as a whole. **Each** followed by **of** plus a pronoun or plural noun (*each of us*, *each of the students*) belongs to a separate entry.",
